{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "No Install Attempted; Add Ruby Orb",
    "Explanation": [
      "The frozen config shows an `orbs:` block containing only the placeholder comment `# Add Orb here`, and the steps list contains only `checkout`, a placeholder comment `# Add step below to install Ruby version 2.6.3`, a blank line, and then `run: ruby -v`. No installation step of any kind (no orb command, no apt-get, no image change) is present, so no installation was attempted. The log confirms this: `ruby: command not found` with exit code 127, which is the shell's 'command not found' status — it is not a timeout, and not a partial/failed install (which would produce package-manager or download errors). The base image `cimg/base:stable` intentionally ships without a language runtime, and the scaffolding of the file (an empty `orbs` stanza plus a step placeholder directly above the version check) signals that the intended remedy is to declare the CircleCI Ruby orb (e.g. `ruby: circleci/ruby@x.y`) and invoke its install command pinned to 2.6.3 in the marked step slot. That places the runtime on PATH before `ruby -v` executes. The other options don't fit the exercise: changing the base image would bypass the orb lesson and pin the version implicitly, apt would not reliably provide 2.6.3, and increasing the timeout addresses a failure mode not observed here."
