{
  "Answer": {
    "Title": "Deploy job lacks a production-only branch filter",
    "Explanation": [
      "The workflow ran on branch `koans-08-branch-filters` (triggered via API), and every job — including `deploy` — finished SUCCESS, so the pipeline is green. However, the requirement is that `deploy` may only run on the `production` branch. The frozen config declares `deploy` in the `build-test-and-deploy` workflow with only a `requires: [test-production]` key and no `filters` block, so there is no branch eligibility restriction at all: `deploy` executes on every branch whose upstream jobs succeed. That is exactly what was observed — deploy completed on a non-production branch — so the observed behaviour does not satisfy the requirement, even though nothing failed. `requires` only enforces ordering/dependency, not branch scoping, so relying on it is insufficient; and branch filters in CircleCI are not honoured inside the job definition under `jobs:` — they must be specified on the job's entry within the `workflows:` stanza. The correct fix is to attach a `filters: branches: only: production` block to the `deploy` entry in the workflow, which makes the deploy job's branch eligibility explicit and restricted to production. The `build` and `test-production` jobs should keep running on all branches, so no change is needed there."
    ],
